  "step_2": "The individual states: 'Alle Felder aufgedeckt. Gewinn bei Lotterie A war garantiert, daher wurde A gewählt.' This translates to: 'All fields uncovered. The win in lottery A was guaranteed, therefore A was chosen.' The individual explicitly notes that A offers a guaranteed win, which is a key feature of A. There is no mention of probabilities of outcomes, no discussion of skewness, no reference to the distribution of outcomes (e.g., 80% vs. 20%), nor any evaluation of the shape of the probability distribution. The justification is based solely on the certainty of the outcome in A, not on any consideration of skewness. The individual does not consider the possibility of higher returns in B or the distribution of outcomes in terms of skewness. The deliberation process is based on risk (certainty vs. risk), not on the skewness of the distributions.",
  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason (skewness) is not considered by the individual. The individual does not mention the distribution of outcomes or compare the shape of the probability mass. The justification is based on certainty, not on skewness. The decision reason requires evaluating which lottery has a greater portion of probability on favorable outcomes (i.e., left-skewness), but the individual only notes that A is certain. Since the individual does not consider skewness and instead relies on risk aversion or certainty, the decision reason was not used. Therefore, the individual did not apply the skewness-based reasoning to make the decision.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
